[Music]  6 40 here on a wednesday morning we  usually have our morning cup of joe  segment with sheriff joe lombardo on  wednesdays he's running for governor as  you know so now  it's mornings with metro and today we  are joined by undersheriff christopher  darcy good to see you sir how are you  doing this morning i'm doing great thank  you for having me on the show and thank  you for being here  let's talk about one of the main issues  we've been covering recently a case ever  at a legion stadium  had his first big concert over the  weekend show went pretty well but  afterwards there was an incident  involving a couple of officers and a  suspect that  they were trying to arrest the suspect  got  his hand on one of the officers guns  opened fire i get that the officers are  going to be okay but just kind of what's  the latest on  on the case right now yes thank you so  much for asking about our officers too  it's very important we appreciate the  community support  so they're home resting obviously one  was struck by the bullet in the leg and  the other one was hit from some  splashback from the round hitting the  ground  essentially they took the suspect into  custody for pushing a security officer  they had him in handcuffs and were  escorting him into an elevator the  handcuffs were  tight or not appropriately placed so  they were readjusting them right to make  sure that the suspect was  cuffed appropriately and at that point  he was able to reach back around  stick his finger into the holster of the  firearm and a round discharge  striking the officer so with something  like that obviously we go back and we'll  do a review  whether it was equipment whether it's  training or whether it's a policy issue  well you know yesterday at the press  conference uh metro had mentioned that  this was going to be reviewed whether  it's an equipment issue or a malfunction  of some kind but  this is i believe the second time that  there's been a a case like this where a  suspect  has gotten their hand on a gun that was  the the amari nicholson suspect  terrell rhodes i believe and that was in  a different circumstance but still was  able to get a hand on the  on their gun presumably there are  traitors training and  things to try and prevent that from  happening correct would that just not  come through what happened yes that well  they're two different incidents so we'll  look at each one separately and  determine like i said whether it's a  tactical issue or an equipment issue or  a policy issue that we need to change  um in the first case you're referring to  was in an interview room with two  detectives where the gun was actually  removed from the holster and a struggle  ensued and i'm happy to say that our  officers didn't use deadly force or  anything they were able to get the  firearm away from the suspect  and in this case the gun never actually  came out of the holster  so that the round discharged while the  gun was inside the holster so the two  different  set of circumstances but it does merit  us taking a very comprehensive review  like i said on our training and our  tactics and equipment so  speaking of allegiant and the big crowds  we had in town for the fourth of july  there was a big relaunch a big  enforcement effort on the las vegas trip  downtown to try and make sure that  any sort of crime was snuffed out before  it got bad  talk about those enforcement efforts and  whether metro considers  they went well uh it did go well i mean  it was a very very busy weekend  as we look back at all the different  events that were going on the concerts  and the the event at allegiant stadium  the electric edc type festival and  everything that we had  um it was a very very busy weekend um  and i i anticipate that we could  probably continue to see that as we move  forward right  well especially when this strip started  to reopen in the first place remember  there were a lot of fights and there was  some gun violence on the strips i  imagine it's a pretty big effort by  metro to try and  make sure that doesn't come back yes and  as we've talked about before the  operation persistent pressure that we  run down to convention center area  command  really it's a partnership between all  the security of all the different  properties and all the different law  enforcement agencies in this community  really  assist us in that we couldn't do it  alone there's a lot of officers that we  need out there and i'm happy to say  that we haven't had a shooting on the  strip in three months so  our efforts are paying off we're still  retrieving  some guns from people on the strip but  not nearly as many as we were  several months ago so that continual  contact and pressure on the strip with  our partners is making a difference to  keep  las vegas safe now in addition you  mentioned partnerships there's also a  big partnership during the fourth to  track  down illegal fireworks use yes that's  not a new issue in las vegas or anywhere  else for the 4th of july  this year was a little bit different  talk about what metro did with other law  enforcement agencies and fire  departments  yes to keep an eye on those fireworks  yeah we partner with the city and the  county fire department and we go out and  i think we responded to over  650 wow we got 650 calls we responded to  about 140 of them  we impounded over 1700 pounds of  fireworks and  i mean we don't get them all right as we  know we live in the neighborhoods and we  hear them but  we made a good effort this year to try  to stop some of those fires that you had  mentioned earlier in your newscast  it's got to be hard to try and just find  them i mean it's you see them in the sky  but trying to find where they are  i mean it's got to be a needle in a  haystack it is and often when  officers go down into a neighborhood  street they run into the house or they  hide or they move they're not generally  standing outside all the time but  you know we can conduct an investigation  and determine where it came from and  issue appropriate citations right well  undersheriff christopher darcy we  appreciate you joining us this morning  here from mornings with metro  if you have a question for metro police  yourself you can submit it on our  website of course  it's eight news now dot com you can find  any for questions answered every  wednesday

